{
  "summary": "This pull request configures CMake's `check_cxx_source_compiles_with_flags()` to treat compiler warnings as errors, preventing check passes when unknown arguments are passed. It also changes the compiler flag for x86 SHA-NI crypto code from `-msse4` to `-msse4.1`. The latter reflects the actual intrinsics used and allows the flag to be recognized by `clang-cl`.",
  "problem": "During build feature detection, `check_cxx_source_compiles_with_flags()` does not treat compiler warnings (such as `-Wunknown-argument`) as errors, which can cause unsupported flags to falsely pass detection. Additionally, `-msse4` is rejected by the `clang-cl` frontend and unnecessarily implies SSE4.2 when the SHA-NI code only relies on SSE4.1 intrinsics.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author description: \"This is a prerequisite for #31507\" (native Windows builds using clang-cl).",
    "Author description: \"-msse4 is merely a synonym for -msse4.2 in both GCC and Clang, but it is not accepted by the clang-cl frontend. Furthermore, the x86 SHA-NI code uses only SSE4.1 intrinsics and no SSE4.2 ones.\""
  ],
